/*!
\page p_prerequisite_knowledge Prerequisite Knowledge

New hardware like the Playstation 3 and Xbox 360 has introduced many 
complexities. To use the math library most effectively, it is important to 
have some background information on how this affects the API, its implementation and 
the way you ought to write your math code. Without this background, not only will 
our math library surprise you and cause problems, you will also write code that 
won't have near the performance it can achieve.

In particular, it is important to have some knowledge on the following subjects.
- \ref p_vectorization "Vectorization"
- \ref p_scalar_access "Scalar Access"
- \ref p_load_hit_store "Load Hit Store (LHS)"
- \ref p_branching "Branching"

*/

